# Toolchain / code-generation features (Polly + Clang LTO + aggressive inlining)
# ============================================================================
# The build itself runs on a Polly-enabled AOSP clang (clang-r596125); these
# options switch on what the Makefile hooks expect (see the CONFIG_LLVM_POLLY
# and CONFIG_INLINE_OPTIMIZATION blocks in the top-level Makefile).
#
#   POLLY    - polyhedral loop optimizer: rewrites kernel loops for cache
#              locality and vectorisation. Needs a toolchain built WITH Polly
#              (apt.llvm.org clang does not ship it; AOSP clang does) - the CI
#              runs a Polly sanity check before the build.
#   LTO      - whole-kernel link-time optimization, done with ld.lld
#              (--lto-O3 at link time).
#   THINLTO  - ThinLTO variant: nearly the same codegen as full LTO but with
#              per-module parallel backends, so the link step stays sane.
#   INLINE   - raises the inliner/unroller thresholds, which is what the
#              sibling Kinesis build uses.
#
# If the kernel ever needs to be built with a non-Polly toolchain, drop
# CONFIG_LLVM_POLLY (and, to be safe, disable CONFIG_INLINE_OPTIMIZATION).

# ── Polly ──
CONFIG_LLVM_POLLY=y

# ── Clang LTO (ThinLTO) ──
CONFIG_LTO_CLANG=y
CONFIG_THINLTO=y

# ── Aggressive inlining ──
CONFIG_INLINE_OPTIMIZATION=y
